   `kernel::sliver_kernel::check_sliver_lowering` is sound.

   This file is HAND-WRITTEN (Kernel.lean is generated by regen.sh and must
   not be edited). Phase 7 (TermCheck.lean) related the TERM a bundle
   carries to the solver's DAG. This file relates the EXTENDED query —
   arrays (`select` through store chains) and uninterpreted calls, as loom
   asks it — to the closed core that `check_term_dag` takes: the core must
   be the read-over-write + Ackermann + congruence elimination of the
   extended query along the untrusted map and the untrusted read / call
   tables, and the check verifies every entry of that advice.

   The semantics: an extended model is an input assignment `inp0`, an
   array interpretation `arrs : Arrs` (every array id a total map
   BV32 → BV8) and a UF interpretation `ufs : Ufs` (every function id a
   total map from argument values; a call node coerces the result to its
   declared width, so one `ufs` interprets every signature). `extSim` is
   `dagSim` with two more arms (`extNodeVal`'s `Core` arm IS
   `dagNodeVal`), `ExtSat` says every asserted root is true.

   Proof architecture:
   * `pWalk` is the pure mirror of the chain walk (`chain_walk_loop_spec`),
     `pBitsEq` / `pExtConst` / `pImpl` / `pAnte` mirror the other total
     helpers; the congruence-root loops are specified by the two-sided
     `ArrCong` / `UfCong` (every root after the extended roots' images is
     an expected congruence root, and every expected pair has its root).
   * `SliverCorr` is everything syntactic an accepted run establishes:
     the per-node correspondence (`ExtNodeCorr`), the injectivity of the
     map on extended variables, the two tables (`ReadTable` / `CallTable`),
     the disjointness of the three variable classes and the LIVENESS of
     every table entry (`SelMapsTo` / `CallMapsTo`): some extended select
     / call reaches it.
   * `sliver_corr_values` is the induction over the extended nodes turning
     it into value equality under `ExtVarsAgree` and a base-read / base-call
     hypothesis that may use the induction hypothesis below the node — so
     the ONE induction serves both transports: with `TablesAgree` (the
     pullback direction) and with the pushforward construction (whose read
     variables are defined on the EXTENDED side, from the first select
     that reaches the entry: its index precedes the select in node order,
     so the induction reaches it first — no recursion through the core
     assignment, which is why the kernel need not order an entry's index
     against its variable; a DEAD entry, which nothing reaches, is what
     the kernel rejects, since its index may mention its own variable and
     its congruence roots could then refute the core alone).
   * `pushforward_sat` (UNSAT direction: every congruence root is VALID
     under `TablesAgree` — Ackermann's functional consistency is the only
     theory fact) and `pullback_tables_agree` (SAT direction: the
     congruence set is COMPLETE, which makes the interpretation built by
     classical choice over "the first entry with this index / argument
     value" well defined; a skipped pair is two constants with unequal
     bits, whose values differ).
   * The capstones compose with the UNCHANGED `check_term_dag` /
